    "adviceC": "Allow extra travel time",
    "incidentKind": "Unplanned",
    "mainCategory": "EMERGENCY ROADWORK",
    "lastUpdated": 1794761673439,
    "otherAdvice": "<p><strong>Great Western Hwy is open between Lithgow and Little Hartley. </strong>The highway is closed between Coxs River Rd and Victoria St.</p><p>Images will be provided within the Attachments sect",
    "arrangementElements": [],
    "diversions": "<p><strong>Eastbound: </strong>Chifley Rd and Darling Causeway.</p><p><strong>Westbound:</strong> Harley Ave, Darling Causeway, Chifley Rd.</p><p>Allow extra travel time. <strong>If travelling during peak periods (Monday to Thursday 8:30 to 10am and 2 to 3:30pm, and Friday 8:30am to 3:30pm), you may need to allow around an additional hour of travel time.\u00a0</strong></p><p>Through traffic on Great Western Hwy can consider alternative routes such as the Golden Hwy or Hume Hwy.</p><ul><li>Detour is suitable for general access vehicles up to 19 metres long and Performance Based Standards (PBS) Level 1 heavy vehicles up to 20 metres long</li><li>Restricted access heavy vehicle operators who are unable to travel on an approved Notice Network are advised to reroute their journeys.</li><li>Restricted access heavy vehicle operators who are unable to travel on a Notice Network are\u00a0advised to apply\u00a0for an amended permit via NHVR Go.\u00a0</li><li><strong>Please note that Class 1 Oversize and/or Over Mass (OSOM) vehicles and Special Purpose Vehicles (SPV) cannot currently be accommodated on the Chifley Rd/Darling Causeway detour route.\u00a0</strong></li><li>To check approved Notice Networks, heavy vehicle operators can use the NHVR National Network Map to find an alternative route for their combination: <a href=\"https://www.nhvr.gov.au/road-access/route-planner/national-network-map\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.nhvr.gov.au/road-access/route-planner/national-network-map</a></li></ul><p>Operators who require a NHVR issued Permit are reminded that they must only travel on the roads approved in their Permit.</p>",
